{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Whose eye is seen eye to eye, You are YHWH</b> – Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 14:14): it concerns the appearance of the glory of YHWH before the eyes of the children of Israel (Exodus 24:17). <b>נִרְאָה</b> is a passive verb, and its meaning is 'You are seen.' And similarly, ״וְנֵאשֲׁאַר אָנִי״ (Ezekiel 9:8), and similarly, ״כִּי אֻמְלַל אָנִי״ (Psalms 6:3), because the lamed has a major pataḥ:" "And the doubling of <b>עַיִן בְּעַיִן</b> — the commentators said: in the manner of people whose eyes see His eyes when He speaks with them, and similarly, ״Face to face, YHWH spoke with you״ (Deuteronomy 5:4). And by way of truth, <b>עַיִן</b> has the sense of appearance: ״And its appearance עֵינוֹ is like the appearance of bedolach״ (Numbers 11:7), ״And I saw what looked like כְּעֵין the appearance of ḥashmal״ (Ezekiel 1:27). He says: that which appears in an appearance is seen — this is Your great name. And similarly the subject of the verse in Ezekiel (43:3): ״And like the appearance of the appearance that I saw, like the appearance that I saw when I came to destroy the city, and appearances like the appearance that I saw by the river Kevar.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:32.837325980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}